# Without this, `COPY . .` drops the host's .venv into the image on top of the
# one the builder just created. On a Windows or macOS checkout those are
# binaries for the wrong platform entirely, and they land at exactly the path
# the container runs from — a build that succeeds and an image that cannot
# start. It is also 400MB+ of pure waste on every layer and every push.
.venv/
venv/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Not needed at runtime, and each one invalidates the layer cache when touched.
tests/
docs/
designs/

# Markdown is deliberately NOT excluded wholesale: the seed registry is a .md
# file that scripts/seed.py parses, so a blanket *.md rule makes seeding inside
# the container fail with a confusing "registry not found".

*.log
.DS_Store
docker-compose.yml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
